14) Local dev instructions (Windows / PC)
Clone or place the project folder on your PC.

In PowerShell inside the project root:

# allow scripts for this session only (safe)
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -Force

npm install
npm run dev
Open http://localhost:3000

To test the serverless API locally, use Vercel CLI or emulate:

Easiest for local test: run node on the function (but that requires minor tweaks)

Alternatively, use curl or Postman against the Vercel-deployed URL after you deploy

15) Deploy to Vercel (recommended steps)
Push the repo to GitHub.

In Vercel, import the repo.

Vercel will auto-detect Vite. Set:

Build Command: npm run build

Output Directory: dist

In Vercel → Settings → Environment Variables, add:

AUDIT_API_KEY (if you want to protect endpoint)

AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID, AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY, AWS_REGION, AWS_S3_BUCKET (if using S3)

Deploy. The endpoint will be:

POST https://your-vercel-domain/api/audit-log
